      <p>
        I've been riding motorcycles over the years for various reasons. It was mostly a daily commute for
        me back when I was living in Turkey. After a long break since I moved to the US in 2015, I
        finally decided to get back to it and get a motorcycle, this time mostly for recreation.
      </p>
      <p>
        So I took some classes like <a href="https://slccmotorcycleregistration.com/returning-riders">the returning rider course</a>
        from community college to help remember riding. Then I bought a
        <a href="https://www.harley-davidson.com/us/en/motorcycles/fat-boy.html">Harley-Davidson Fat Boy 114</a>.
        It's substantially larger than my previous bikes—~700lbs (317kg) with a 114ci (1868cc) engine—so I was a bit nervous,
        but it’s been a smooth experience. I often use it to go to the gym or ride around with my wife (season permitting).
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

